    "answer": {
      "short": "The working is correct. Recognise $\\sin(2\\theta-\\theta)=\\sin\\theta$ directly using the sine difference identity.",
      "worked": "The working is correct, but the sine difference identity gives a shorter method:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin 2\\theta\\cos\\theta-\\cos 2\\theta\\sin\\theta&=\\sin(2\\theta-\\theta)\\\\\\sin 2\\theta\\cos\\theta-\\cos 2\\theta\\sin\\theta&=\\sin\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
